  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This code stores the word HELLO, scan it, and the reader rebuilds HELLO. Now, cover some of these central squares. How can the message survive? A QR code stores extra error correction information alongside the message. Watch the reader use that information to work out what the missing values should be. The reader fills in those missing values, and HELLO is recovered. The large corner patterns have another job, helping the reader find and align the code. But repair has a limit. Cover too much data and the reader no longer has enough information to rebuild the message. Error correction gives the reader a second chance to recover the message.",
